[[Phosani's Nightmare]] is a solo boss located in the [[Sisterhood Sanctuary]], a dungeon beneath [[Slepe]] in [[Morytania]]. It is the stronger version of [[the Nightmare]].

Players can initiate the fight by entering the [[Pool of Nightmares]] which is located north of The Nightmare's arena on a raised area. As a solo instanced fight, players do not need to hop worlds.

Phosani's Nightmare awakens in 10 seconds upon entering the instance, compared to 30 at the original. After she is defeated, players can continue fighting her by disturbing her again.

Unlike most other bosses, players who die fighting Phosani's Nightmare are sent back outside to the Pool of Nightmares, and [[Sister Senga]] acts as an [[Item Retrieval Service]] for this purpose. Reclaims cost {{Coins|60000}} regardless of the equipment's value or amount of kills completed.

==Requirements==
*Completion of {{SCP|Quest}} [[Priest in Peril]] to access [[Morytania]].

==Recommendations==
*High [[combat]] stats. Although not required, see the skill levels below for an indication of the advised stats:
**Level {{SCP|Attack|95}} or higher
**Level {{SCP|Strength|95}} or higher
**Level {{SCP|Defence|85}} or higher
**Level {{SCP|Magic|95}} or higher
**Level {{SCP|Hitpoints|95}} or higher
**Level {{SCP|Prayer|70}} or higher
*Completion of {{SCP|Quest}} [[A Taste of Hope]] for the [[Drakan's Medallion]], which is the quickest teleportation method.
**Alternatively, completion of {{SCP|Quest}} [[Ghosts Ahoy]] for the [[ectophial]], which is the second quickest teleportation method.

==Transportation==
The five quickest methods of reaching [[Slepe]], where Phosani's Nightmare resides, are (from fastest to slowest):
*Teleporting directly to Slepe via [[Drakan's medallion]] after unlocking this teleport via [[Slepey tablet]], which is a drop from Phosani's Nightmare.
*Teleporting to the [[Morytania Spider Cave]] with a [[spider cave teleport]] and running east to Slepe
*Teleporting to [[Hallowed Sepulchre]] using a [[Hallowed crystal shard]], then running east to Slepe via an agility shortcut that requires 63 [[Agility]] and installing two [[Long rope]]s
*Teleporting to [[Ver Sinhaza]] via [[Drakan's medallion]], then running north. Once players pass the small dock, run east to arrive at Slepe.
*Using the [[Ectophial]] to teleport to the [[Ectofuntus]], then heading north to the small dock and paying [[Andras]] 10,000 coins to row to Slepe. The player will arrive at a dock just south-west of Slepe.

==Mechanics==
Phosani's Nightmare shares the same combat stats with the original, despite having a higher combat level.

The fight is divided into four phases; three normal phases with a shield value of 400 and a final phase consisting of 150 hitpoints, along with four totems in the first three phases with a charge value of 200 (100 if maging).

The total amount of physical damage needed is 1,350, while totem charges needed are 2,400 (1,200 if maging); a total of 2,550 damage is required.

===Standard attacks===
[[File:The Nightmare - attacks.mp4|thumb|400px|A player correctly praying against the Nightmare's attacks.|autoplay|loop]]
Unlike the normal Nightmare, praying against the attacks of Phosani's Nightmare will fully block damage. However, the attacks deal significantly increased damage in return if not protected against, with both the ranged and magic having a maximum hit of 80 and melee a maximum of 73.
*[[Ranged]] attack: Phosani's Nightmare will contort herself and shoot out projectiles toward players; having game sounds enabled will help as this attack performs a loud clicking sound per contortion. Players have '''3 ticks''' (1.8s) to react with [[Protect from Missiles]].
*[[Magic]] attack: Phosani's Nightmare will flail to the side surrounding herself with pink flower petals, then spin back shooting the petals toward players. Players have '''3 ticks''' (1.8s) to react with [[Protect from Magic]].
*[[Melee]] attack: Phosani's Nightmare will charge her claws and quickly scrapes the area in front of her. Players have '''2 ticks''' (1.2s) to react with [[Protect from Melee]]. This attack will always hit regardless of the player's defensive bonuses if not protected against. The attack can also be avoided by walking one tile away from her just before the claws rise up.

===Special attacks===
Each phase will have three special attacks. This will always consist of one "spawn" (husk or parasite), one paired with Grasping Claws (Corpse Flowers or Spores), and one miscellaneous special attack (Curse or Surge). Below are four possible sets of special attacks:

* '''A1''': Spore/Husks/Curse
* '''A2''': Spore/Husks/Surge
* '''B1''': Flowers/Parasite/Curse
* '''B2''': Flowers/Parasite/Surge

The first phase picks a random set (A or B), then every following phase alternates between the A and B sets, but randomly picks between 1 and 2. For example, a special attack set will go as follows: A1, B2, A2.

The Nightmare '''will''' expend all special attacks first before she may use them again, and both the spawning mechanic and claw-accompanying mechanic cannot be used in consecutive phases.
* '''Sleepwalkers:''' At the end of the first three phases, Phosani's Nightmare will summon [[Sleepwalker (Phosani's Nightmare)|sleepwalkers]] that walk toward her, the number of which is dependent upon which phase the player is on, up to four at the end of phase three.
** Sleepwalkers have 10 health, but players will deal their maximum hit on them and always hit regardless of bonuses. The number of sleepwalkers that reach her will determine how strong her power blast will be. If no sleepwalkers are killed, the resulting blast will always kill the player.
[[File:The Nightmare - husks.mp4|thumb|400px|The Nightmare summons a pair of husks.]]
* '''Husks:''' Phosani's Nightmare spawns two [[Husk (Phosani's Nightmare)|husks]] around the player. The player will be frozen in place until the husks are killed. The blue, skinny husk uses magic attacks, while the green, bulky husk uses ranged attacks.
** Phosani's Nightmare will not spawn Grasping Claws portals under players frozen by the husks. '''However, if the player is under Phosani's Nightmare while frozen by husks, they will still take damage'''. Additionally, any weapon on its crush attack style will always land as a [[maximum hit]] on the husks.
** To fully avoid damage from husks, kill the ranged husk first during phases 1 and 2. The magic husk will hit before the Nightmare does, whereas the ranged husk will hit on the same tick as the Nightmare.
** During phase 3, if the Nightmare uses melee, the magic husk must be killed first, as damage will register on the same tick.
* '''Spores:''' Puffshroom-like objects spawn around the arena. Standing within 1 tile of one will cause it to explode, causing the player to become weary; their run is disabled, their attack speed is lowered by 2 ticks, and every yawn will also drain prayer by 6 points. Accompanied by '''Grasping Claws''', the attack will occur before or after husks appear.
* '''Parasites:''' Phosani's Nightmare impregnates the player with a [[parasite (Phosani's Nightmare)|parasite]]. After ~18 ticks (10.8s), it will grow and burst out of the player, dealing massive damage, and will then begin healing Phosani's Nightmare until killed. 
** Drinking a dose of [[Sanfew serum]] or [[Relicym's balm]] before it emerges will weaken the parasite and greatly reduce the damage taken when the parasite bursts out; like with husks, any weapon on its crush attack style will always hit as a maximum hit against a weakened parasite. Players may click the [[Minimap|Hitpoints Orb]] to weaken the Parasite instead of clicking the potion within their inventory as well.
[[File:The Nightmare - corpse flowers.mp4|thumb|400px|The Nightmare's Corpse Flower attack, followed by her Grasping Claws attack.]]
*'''Corpse Flowers:''' Phosani's Nightmare will divide the room into four equal quadrants with lines of flowers. One quadrant will be safe as indicated with white '''nightmare flowers''', while the remaining quadrants are unsafe as indicated with red '''nightmare berries'''. Accompanied by '''Grasping Claws''', the attack will occur before or after the parasite appears.
** If the player is in the incorrect quadrant, they will take rapid damage that heals the boss for twice the amount inflicted, and any attacks that would damage the boss will instead heal her.

The following special attacks are used randomly throughout all phases.
* '''Grasping Claws:''' Phosani's Nightmare will spawn a black portal underneath her, and numerous smaller "end" portals before sticking her claws inside. If the player stands on '''any''' portal, they will take up 50-65 damage. Simply move into a tile free of a black portal to avoid damage. Compared to the normal fight, Grasping Claws is significantly more clumped around the player, as well as being used several times in succession instead of once.
** This attack is used randomly throughout the fight, and is also performed for the entirety of the '''Corpse Flowers''' and '''Spores''' attacks. Lastly, it is used indefinitely during her desperation phase.
*'''Curse:''' A pink glow fills the player's screen and protection prayers are shuffled to the right. Using [[Protect from Melee]] will instead activate [[Protect from Magic]], Protect from Magic activates [[Protect from Missiles]], and Protect from Missiles activates Protect from Melee. After 5 attacks, the curse is lifted.
*'''Surge:''' Phosani's Nightmare will teleport to one of the four edges of the room, then immediately surge across to the opposite side, dealing up to ~80 damage if caught in her path. Move out of the way to avoid taking damage.
*'''Prayer Deactivation:''' Only during phase three, Phosani's Nightmare will deactivate the player's protection prayer if they have the correct prayer active before the attack animation starts.

==Fight overview==
Before heading to the boss, eat an [[anglerfish]] to overheal. If the player does not have the teleport to the [[Sisterhood Sanctuary]] with [[Drakan's medallion]] (via [[slepey tablet]], acquired from the boss), it is '''required''' that players sip a [[stamina potion]] before leaving the bank, as their run energy will deplete before even reaching the sanctuary. If the player has the teleport unlocked, a stamina dose is not necessary.

The fight plays out very similarly to the original, though much faster. Phosani's Nightmare is significantly more punishing when a mistake is made, as its auto-attacks have the capability to kill players in two hits. Food that can heal 22 (ideally anglerfish for its overhealing capability) is recommended for mistakes and chip damage taken during the fight. Unlike the original, an [[amulet of blood fury]] is not mandatory, as an ideal kill will only see minor chip damage, dealt through phase transitions and parasites. Generally without a [[saradomin godsword]], up to three mistakes are allowed, after which the fourth one will likely kill the player when accounting for the best loadout.

When using a weapon on its crush setting, the player will be guaranteed a maximum hit on both husks and weakened parasites. When using a 5-tick or slower weapon such as a [[scythe of Vitur]], a [[goblin paint cannon]] or [[ham joint]] swap is generally encouraged due to their 3-tick attack speed. If using an 4-tick weapon such as an [[inquisitor's mace]], this is not necessary. For parasites, the player must have a minimum of 118 [[Strength]], a strength bonus of 160 or more and [[piety]] in order to one-hit weakened parasites. A godsword swap requires piety and a four-way swap of the weapon, cape, amulet and gloves. If the parasite is not weakened, the damage it deals to the player will be added onto its base health, and the player will not be able to land maximum hits on it even with crush weapons. An elder maul will not need any swaps, but the strength level and piety must be maintained.
[[File:Phosani's Nightmare - corner rifting.mp4|thumb|400px|A player demonstrates the corner rifting technique, using audio cues to time their movements.]]
Learning players will likely struggle against the Grasping Claws, as a late reaction by even a tick will deal heavy damage, and it also has the capability to kill players in two hits. It is important to quickly locate safe tiles; learners should prioritise dodging the pools over attacking the boss, as a few mistakes will quickly kill the player. A more advanced strategy is to "corner rift"; this method requires the player to stand underneath the Nightmare by the corners of her collision box, as standing anywhere else will result in damage. The player must quickly step out of the boss before the next set of pools form, or one will form in the corner. This allows players to maintain a cadence while minimising tick loss from not attacking the boss.

Before using Flower Power or Spores,{{Fact}} the Nightmare will have a slight delay before actually using the attack alongside Grasping Claws. She will always teleport to the centre of the arena when performing these attacks.

As with the original fight, there are three iterations of Flower Power. Assuming she is not moved from the centre, two of these layouts will not require the player to move her. Some particular layouts will have spores diagonally across from her, which requires luring her away from the centre as they will severely restrict movement. If the player is tick perfect, they can move her two tiles south to corner rift; if the boss only moves one tile due to late reactions, corner rifting is still not possible but the area east and south of the boss can be used to dodge rifts.

At the end of each phase, the Nightmare will spawn a corresponding amount of [[Sleepwalker (Phosani's Nightmare)|sleepwalkers]] while charging up an attack. This attack will '''always''' deal 149 damage if no sleepwalkers are killed. Killing a sleepwalker will reduce the damage appropriately to the amount of sleepwalkers present; e.g with 4 sleepwalkers, each sleepwalker killed will reduce the blast damage by 36. If all sleepwalkers are killed before they reach the boss, the blast will deal 5 damage instead. Sleepwalker control can be dealt with using [[blisterwood stake]]s or a [[toxic blowpipe]] on the [[rapid]] style, but quick reactions must be maintained to avoid leaks.

