=== Phases 1-2 ===
The first two phases are very much like the regular encounter except the special attacks can be used randomly in any of these phases.

As the player progresses through the phases, sleepwalkers will spawn in to reach the Nightmare. Two will spawn at the end of phase 1 and an additional will spawn at the end of the phase.

=== Phase 3 ===
Phosani's Nightmare will deactivate the player's protection prayers as soon as she starts her attack animation. Since the attacks have a slight delay and only deal damage upon being launched, this is mostly to keep players vigilant. She will also have a much higher chance of using melee attacks during this time, so players should prioritise activating Protect from Melee (or Ranged if Curse is active).

To avoid damage from husks during the phase, players should not have any overhead prayers active before they appear. Once the husks appear, pray magic, as both the Nightmare and the magic husk will attack on the same tick (although the magic husk will hit first). If the player prays against magic and the Nightmare uses a magic attack, the magic husk will likely hit the player. Even if the Nightmare uses melee, players can still flick against all three enemies at once by praying against magic, then melee and finally ranged within 1 tick of each other from the first prayer.

For sleepwalker control in this phase, players using a short ranged weapon like blisterwood stakes should stand next to one corner of the arena, as a sleepwalker is guaranteed to spawn on either side of the pillar. If using a bow, stand in the middle. Unlike the previous phase, there is a slight delay before the sleepwalkers start moving. '''In order to avoid damage from sleepwalkers, the player must kill at least two sleepwalkers before this delay lifts.'''

===Desperation phase===
[[File:Phosani's Nightmare - desperation phase.mp4|thumb|450px|Mastering corner rifting, unleashing special attacks at the end, and having Redemption active, can mean the difference between finishing the fight and dying.<br/><br/>Here, the player fails to kill the last sleepwalker, and has run out of food and prayer potions. However, having Redemption active allowed them to take one more power blast and finish off the fight by the skin of their teeth.]]
Phosani's Nightmare will survive the final blast, and teleport to the centre of the arena. Lashing out to survive, she will unleash a desperate last stand by indefinitely using '''Grasping Claws''', while sleepwalkers continuously spawn from the edges of the arena. Mastering the corner rifting technique will make this phase less hectic.

Unlike the previous sleepwalkers, these will only deal 15 damage upon reaching the Nightmare, with a short delay. The first sleepwalker that spawns will deal damage ~20 ticks after spawning, allowing for four attacks with a four or five-tick weapon before this occurs. Focusing on ending the fight instead of dealing with the sleepwalkers is crucial.

Before the phase starts, the player should fully restore their health, ensure their melee stats are boosted, and their special attack energy is full. Although not necessary, standing underneath the boss before the phase starts will usually allow the player to dodge the first set of rifts. Immediately dump special attacks on the Nightmare to quickly damage her, if available. [[Redemption]], although not needed, can be very useful in this phase if low on supplies or if the phase takes longer than usual.

The strongest special attack weapon to use is the [[crimson kisten]], as it is very likely to hit and generally deals more damage on average compared to a [[voidwaker]]. Voidwaker is still strong for players who don't have a kisten, due to its guaranteed accuracy. If neither are available, [[dragon claws]] can perform relatively well despite the boss's high Slash defence, and finally, the [[Granite maul (ornate handle)|ornate granite maul]]. While the maul should be better than dragon claws, it does require proper timing to avoid unnecessary tick delay.

===Hallowfell===

Utilizing the [[Hallowfell]] to its full potential takes some planning to avoid the 1/6 bad husk spawn and 1/4 bad parasite spawn chances. The same trick will work for both situations; when standing next to a wall or against a corner, she cannot spawn either husk or parasite in a location that the Hallowfell will fail to provide area-of-effect damage. However, it is important to note that to effectively move the boss the player needs to be moving in between attacks or waiting for '''Surge''', as both the magic and ranged auto-attacks have a rather lengthy animation that roots her in place.

